## Problem classes

### `Peer missing on Windows`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Other platforms see this machine; Windows does not appear | Firewall blocked UDP 5353, or Bonsoir broadcast failed to start. Windows uses the same Bonsoir path (`DnsServiceRegister` / WinDNS). | Check the advertise log and the private-network firewall prompt. Manual connect remains if multicast is blocked. Do not put Windows back on a browse-only early return. |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Nearby badge says Same LAN but transfers fail`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Subnet match treated as reachable. Refresh still shows a trusted peer as Same LAN after the other phone leaves, until the row is deleted | `/hello` never ran, or a stored host still sits in a reused private CIDR (`192.168.0.0/24` on two different networks). Trusted rows are not purged, and a refresh that only retries already-stale rows never re-checks them. A BLE advert IPv4 from the last scan is fresher than the stored host | Same LAN only when the newest address (BLE advert IPv4 when present) is on a current subnet and a recent `/hello` succeeded. Refresh and a short timer re-hello on-subnet peers, trusted ones included. An advert address outside the current subnets marks the row stale and moves it off the list without deleting trust. Restart the BLE advert when this phone's own IPv4 changes so the other side sees the move |

